s4-4-p37 = prose (cons "For \(n\) distinct elements, the fiber of list sorting over their sorted sequence consists of the \(n!\) enumerations. Retaining that permutation allows the input enumeration to be recovered; returning only the sorted list forgets it. For repeated values with multiplicities \(m_1,\ldots,m_r\), the number of distinct value sequences is instead \(n!/\prod_jm_j!\). The bag declaration intentionally keeps multiplicities without claiming to keep a particular original enumeration." nil)
